Package: darkniche
Title: Climatic Dark Diversity and Directional Niche Coverage
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", role = "aut"))
Description: A reproducible framework for asking which species are absent
    from a region despite tolerating its climate -- its climatic dark
    diversity. Implements the directional niche-coverage family (DNC_q,
    DNC_auc, NSI, CFI, NOV), which answers containment questions that
    symmetric overlap statistics (Schoener's D, Warren's I) cannot express;
    three analytical null models (breadth-matched, environmental shift,
    geographic relocation); calibrated dark-diversity accounting with an
    area-adjusted dark-diversity ratio; validation against documented
    introduced ranges with fast DeLong tests; and a threshold-sweep
    diagnostic that reveals when the direction of an aggregate null-model
    test is an artefact of the chosen threshold. Publication-quality
    figures and table exporters are included, together with results for
    all 619 terrestrial ecoregions as bundled example data.
